      "text": "To find the value of \\( x \\) that satisfies the equation \\( x^2 = 729 \\), we need to take the square root of both sides of the equation. The square root of a number \\( y \\) is a number \\( z \\) such that \\( z^2 = y \\). Therefore, we have:\n\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt{729}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine the value of \\( \\sqrt{729} \\). We do this by finding the number that, when multiplied by itself, gives 729. We can do this by factorizing 729 into its prime factors:\n\n\\[\n729 = 27 \\times 27 = 3^3 \\times 3^3 = 3^6\n\\]\n\nSo, the square root of 729 is:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{729} = \\sqrt{3^6} = 3^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nSince \\( x \\) is positive, we take the positive square root. Therefore, the value of \\( x \\) is:\n\n\\[\nx = 27\n\\]\n\nPutting the final answer in the required format, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{27}\n\\]",
